&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;About Crunchyroll&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded by fans, Crunchyroll delivers the art and culture of anime to a passionate community. We super-serve over 100 million anime and manga fans across 200+ countries and territories, and help them connect with the stories and characters they crave. Whether that experience is online or in-person, streaming video, theatrical, games, merchandise, events and more, it’s powered by the anime content we all love.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join our team, and help us shape the future of anime!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Manager, Regional Marketing Operations is responsible for turning global and regional marketing priorities into coordinated, localized, production-ready, and successfully delivered marketing activity across the Region.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role owns the regional execution layer of the marketing operating model, connecting Regional Marketing with Crunchyroll’s global operational capabilities. The candidate will ensure campaigns are operationally planned, assets are produced and localized to regional requirements, dependencies are managed, and final materials are delivered accurately and on time across relevant regional channels and partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A critical responsibility of the role is the end-to-end management of marketing localization for the Region. This includes localization of all marketing assets used regionally, whether those assets originate from a global campaign or are created specifically for a regional initiative. The Manager coordinates translation, transcreation, adaptation, versioning, approvals, quality checks, and delivery of localized marketing materials, working closely with Global Localization while remaining accountable for regional marketing localization readiness.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role operates as the regional counterpart to Global Operations, Content and Marketing and Distribution Operations, Content and Marketing, with particularly close interfaces to Integrated Planning, Campaign Operations, Marketing Production, and Marketing Delivery. The objective is to leverage common global processes, technology, production capabilities, and standards while ensuring regional priorities, language requirements, cultural considerations, channels, and market-specific needs are fully represented&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regional Marketing Operations &amp;amp; Execution: Own the operational coordination of the Region’s marketing activity, translating global and regional marketing strategies into executable plans, milestones, asset requirements, localization needs, dependencies, and delivery schedules. Maintain an integrated view of regional marketing readiness and ensure activities move effectively from planning through execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regional Integrated Planning: Partner closely with Integrated Planning to incorporate regional priorities, launches, campaigns, tentpoles, local initiatives, and market requirements into the broader global marketing planning process. Translate global plans into actionable regional timelines while providing early visibility into local requirements, resource constraints, localization lead times, and execution risks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;End-to-End Marketing Localization Management: Manage the localization workflow for all global and regional marketing assets required by the Region, including copy, key art, trailers, video, social assets, paid-media creative, CRM materials, partner assets, promotional content, and other campaign deliverables. Coordinate translation, transcreation, cultural adaptation, versioning, review, approvals, QA, and final delivery, ensuring localized assets are accurate, brand-appropriate, culturally relevant, and available against campaign deadlines. Partner with Global Localization on standards, technology, vendors, workflows, terminology, and quality frameworks while retaining operational accountability for regional marketing localization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Marketing Production Coordination: Partner with Marketing Production to communicate regional production and localization requirements early, define necessary versions and formats, and ensure global source assets are structured to enable efficient regional adaptation. Coordinate requests for region-specific materials where global assets do not meet local needs while avoiding unnecessary duplication of global production capabilities. For regionally originated campaigns, manage the operational interface between regional creative requirements and the appropriate production resources.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Marketing Delivery Coordination: Work closely with Marketing Delivery within Distribution Operations, Content and Marketing to ensure final global and localized marketing assets are packaged, distributed, and made available to the correct regional destinations on time. Coordinate region-specific channel requirements, specifications, deadlines, and partner needs and provide clear escalation when assets are missing, incorrect, delayed, or unable to meet delivery requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regional Stakeholder &amp;amp; Market Coordination: Partner with Regional Marketing, Content, Social, CRM, Paid Media, Partnerships, Brand, PR, and other local stakeholders to consolidate operational requirements and create one coordinated regional view of campaign execution. Ensure stakeholders have clear visibility into asset availability, localization status, production milestones, delivery readiness, risks, and decisions required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regional Campaign &amp;amp; Asset Readiness: Establish clear readiness checkpoints for priority campaigns and launches, validating that required source assets, localized versions, formats, approvals, metadata, specifications, and delivery destinations are complete. Identify risks early and coordinate resolution across Campaign Operations, Marketing Production, Global Localization, Marketing Delivery, and regional teams before they impact campaign activation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regional and Partner-Specific Requirements: Own the operational coordination of marketing requirements unique to the Region, including local platforms, commercial partners, media channels, regulatory considerations, language requirements, cultural adaptations, and market-specific formats. Ensure these requirements are communicated sufficiently early to global teams to allow them to be incorporated efficiently into production and delivery workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operational Issue &amp;amp; Escalation Management: Serve as the regional operational control point when marketing assets, localization, production, or delivery issues threaten campaign execution. Coordinate cross-functional triage, maintain clear accountability through resolution, communicate impact and status to regional stakeholders, and escalate systemic issues to the appropriate global teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performance &amp;amp; Continuous Improvement: Track regional marketing operations performance across campaign readiness, on-time asset availability, localization turnaround, production delivery, error rates, rework, and recurring operational issues. Identify opportunities to simplify workflows, improve global-to-regional handoffs, reduce duplicate work, automate repetitive activity, and strengthen the scalability of Crunchyroll’s marketing operating model.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications &amp;amp; Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience in marketing operations, campaign operations, creative operations, localization, marketing production, media operations, or a related field, ideally within entertainment, streaming, media, technology, or another global consumer business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience managing complex, multi-market marketing campaigns with significant dependencies across planning, creative production, localization, asset management, and delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of marketing localization, including translation, transcreation, cultural adaptation, asset versioning, review and approval workflows, and the operational requirements associated with delivering localized creative at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience coordinating both globally originated campaigns and locally originated marketing activity, with the ability to operate effectively between central capabilities and regional business needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of marketing production workflows across multiple asset types, including digital, video, social, paid media, CRM, partner marketing, and promotional creative.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to coordinate across highly matrixed organizations and establish effective working relationships among regional teams and global functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent project and operational management capabilities, with the ability to manage multiple campaigns, markets, languages, asset types, dependencies, and deadlines simultaneously.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with demonstrated ability to identify execution risks early and drive issues through to resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and stakeholder-management skills, including the ability to influence teams across functions, cultures, and time zones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High attention to detail and a strong commitment to brand consistency, localization quality, executional excellence, and the fan experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience within anime, entertainment, streaming, television, gaming, or another global content-led consumer business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing marketing localization across multiple languages and markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with campaign-management, project-management, digital asset-management, localization-management, and marketing-delivery platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with creative agencies, localization vendors, production partners, media agencies, and external distribution or commercial partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience improving marketing workflows through standardization, automation, operational metrics, and root-cause analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Why you will love working at Crunchyroll&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to getting to work with fun, passionate and inspired colleagues, you will also enjoy the following benefits and perks:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Receive a great compensation package including salary plus performance bonus earning potential, paid annually.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible time off policies allowing you to take the time you need to be your whole self.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous medical, dental, vision, STD, LTD, and life insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health Saving Account HSA program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health care and dependent care FSA&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) plan, with employer match&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employer paid commuter benefit&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support program for new parents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pet insurance and some of our offices are pet friendly!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LifeAtCrunchyroll #LI-Hybrid&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3 data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;About our Values&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We want to be everything for someone rather than something for everyone and we do this by living and modeling our values in all that we do. We value&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Courage. We believe that when we overcome fear, we enable our best selves.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Curiosity. We are curious, which is the gateway to empathy, inclusion, and understanding.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Kaizen. We have a growth mindset committed to constant forward progress.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Service. We serve our community with humility, enabling joy and belonging for others.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Our commitment to diversity and inclusion&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mission of helping people belong reflects our commitment to diversity &amp;amp; inclusion. It&#39;s just the way we do business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are an equal opportunity employer and value diversity at Crunchyroll. Pursuant to applicable law, we do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, age, marital status, veteran status, or disability status.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Crunchyroll, LLC is an independently operated joint venture between US-based Sony Pictures Entertainment, and Japan&#39;s Aniplex, a subsidiary of Sony Music Entertainment (Japan) Inc., both subsidiaries of Tokyo-based Sony Group Corporation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;Questions about Crunchyroll’s hiring process? Please check out our Hiring FAQs:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://help.crunchyroll.com/hc/en-us/articles/360040471712-Crunchyroll-Hiring-FAQs&quot;&gt;https://help.crunchyroll.com/hc/en-us/articles/360040471712-Crunchyroll-Hiring-FAQs&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;Please refer to our&amp;nbsp;Candidate Privacy Policy for more information about how we process your personal information, and your data protection rights: &lt;a href=&quot;https://tbcdn.talentbrew.com/company/22978/v1_0/docs/spe-jobs-privacy-policy-update-for-crpa-dec-21-22.pdf&quot;&gt;https://tbcdn.talentbrew.com/company/22978/v1_0/docs/spe-jobs-privacy-policy-update-for-crpa-dec-21-22.pdf&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please beware of recent scams to online job seekers. Those applying to our job openings will only be contacted directly from ----- email account.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About MarqVision&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Protect and build a future shaped by original ideas, innovations and creativity.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Threats to brand integrity are scaling fast. We&#39;re building the intelligence to scale faster. MarqVision is the brand integrity partner for the world&#39;s most ambitious companies, providing AI-powered detection and enforcement across 1,500+ platforms in 115+ countries. We don&#39;t just flag problems; we eliminate them at scale so brands can grow with confidence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 2020 and backed by SoftBank, Y Combinator, DST Global Partners, HSG, and Salesforce Ventures, we&#39;ve been recognized with an LVMH Innovation Award and named to the Inc. 5000 list of America&#39;s fastest-growing private companies in 2025.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you want to work at the intersection of AI, global commerce, and IP, this is the place.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How You&#39;ll Make an Impact:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Customer Success Manager based in our London office, you&#39;ll own the full lifecycle of a portfolio of MarqVision customers, from onboarding through renewal, acting as their trusted partner and single point of accountability. You’ll work closely with teams across MarqVision to ensure customers get full value from our platform and services, and help brands across the UK and Europe protect and grow with confidence. We&#39;re looking for someone self-motivated and proactive, a natural relationship builder who is comfortable managing multiple senior stakeholders across large, complex organisations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary point of contact for a portfolio of customer accounts across the full lifecycle: onboarding, training, check-in calls, business reviews, feature implementation, and renewals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain relationships at all levels of the customer organisation, including executive sponsors, to understand business priorities and cultivate internal advocacy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively monitor account health, identify risk, and execute mitigation plans, escalating internally when needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive adoption of MarqVision’s offering, ensuring customers are leveraging the functionality available to them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify expansion opportunities and partner with Sales to grow account value&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define timelines, milestones, and success criteria for customer initiatives and see them through to completion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Sales, Operations, Product, Engineering, and specialist teams to address customer requests and strategise account growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the voice of the customer internally, sharing feedback that shapes our product and improves the customer experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of Customer Success and/or Account Management experience within brand protection, ideally managing customers in the UK and European markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience owning renewals and expansions, including multi-stakeholder relationships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to demonstrate strategic thinking to grow partnership value across complex customer organisations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent customer-facing skills: training, coaching, executive-level discussion management, conflict resolution, and the ability to creatively explain and present complex concepts in an easy-to-understand manner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working cross-functionally with colleagues across multiple time zones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills as well as business and technical acumen&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Business fluency in French&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Signal&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with marketplace or platform enforcement programmes (e.g., Amazon Brand Registry and similar)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with enterprise customers or in a high-growth startup environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Become a MarqVisioner&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Holiday to take the time you need, when you need it, plus UK bank holidays&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hybrid work model designed for focus and flexibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Equity in every offer, because you should own a piece of what you&#39;re building&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Private medical and dental insurance, plus parental leave to support your life outside of work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Workplace pension scheme with employer contribution to help you save for the future&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Protect what&#39;s original. Scale what&#39;s possible. At MarqVision, we believe real growth comes with attracting the brightest minds, motivating them to succeed in their position, and ensuring plenty of fun along the way. If you think this position is for you, apply now.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;MarqVision is an equal opportunities employer and encourages applicants of all backgrounds to apply. We welcome applications regardless of age, disability, gender reassignment, marriage and civil partnership, pregnancy and maternity, race, religion or belief, sex, or sexual orientation. We are committed to building a diverse and inclusive workforce that reflects the customers and communities we serve.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you need any reasonable adjustments during the application or interview process, please let us know and we&#39;ll be happy to support you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;Are you an experienced full service Project Manager in the field of clinical trials who’s engaged in addressing the challenges facing the research and development of novel compounds in Oncology. Are you passionate about impacting the health and lives of patients around the world? Do you take a consultative approach to trial management, proving to be a valuable partner in trial operational delivery?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Precision for Medicine are looking to hire a Clinical Project Manager / Senior Clinical Project Manager with experience in Oncology who have managed full service clinical trials within a CRO setting to join our global team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this pivotal role you will have full service oversight for clinical projects across global/regional (ph I-IV) trials, within Oncology.&amp;nbsp; Accountable for clinical project delivery, oversight of all functional departments, and ensuring agreed timelines, scope, cost and quality.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Involved in all study stages, including proposal strategy, development, costing, and bid defence, and seeing studies through the full cycle to completion, managing the client relationship, project team and budget and timelines throughout.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work in a cross-functional team with both internal and external stakeholders, driving quality and coordinating the study team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We offer an amazing high-energy, dedicated, collaborative team members who enjoy a challenge, thrive in the details and flourish in dynamic environments. If you are no stranger to taking charge and seek positive teamwork to deliver extraordinary work, we have an opportunity for you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;How we will keep you busy and support your growth:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will independently lead clinical projects in accordance with the study budget and scope of work. You will use your strong interpersonal and organizational skills to set and achieve objectives in the execution of the projects; both contracted objectives and financial objectives. You may be called upon to run international trials as well.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary point-of-contact liaison with the client to provide excellent customer service, including participation in proposal activities and client presentations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Liaise with Project Team and senior management of both Precision and sponsors, including C level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Handle and lead all aspects of a clinical research trial or trials&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Total project management for all functional areas including data management, safety, clinical, medical monitoring and biostatistics, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare project status updates for clients and management; identifying key deliverables and performance metrics of success and escalation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as an active member of the Project Team with the goal to contribute towards efficient management and execution of trials&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare and reviews protocols and other study documentation such as project plans, inform consents, site contracts and budgets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Requirements:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Degree or similar related life science qualification, or equivalent combination of education and experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience in a full service/global Project Management role working in the CRO industry is essential.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive experience working within Clinical Operations position within a CRO, and at least 4 years full service Project Management experience in a clinical trial setting working for a Clinical Research Organisation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing studies within Oncology&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working understanding of GCP/ICH guidelines and the clinical development process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to drive and availability for domestic and international travel including overnight stays&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be able to communicate effectively in the English language both written and spoken&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong presentation skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven computer skills (MS Office, MS Project, PowerPoint) and software experience (CTMS, eTMF, EDC, IXRS)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to develop positive working relationships with individual and teams internally and externally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated core understanding of medical terminology and clinical trial activities as it relates to the execution of a clinical development plan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Precision for Medicine&#39;s uniquely integrated offering enables the science of precision medicine by combining novel clinical trial designs, industry-leading operational and medical authorities, advanced biomarker and data analytics solutions, and an unequivocal real passion for rare diseases and oncology.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a people focussed CRO with a supportive and collaborative environment which promotes work life balance and encourages team development.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We invite you to learn more about our growing organization serving our clients that are researching ground-breaking cancer therapies. We strive to ensure employees feel appreciated for the contributions they make every single day.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Any data provided as a part of this application will be stored in accordance with our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://nam12.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.precisionmedicinegrp.com%2Fprivacy-policy%2F&amp;amp;data=05%7C01%7Czeta.larcon%40precisionmedicinegrp.com%7Cb58fe8b0c3ea4dd2e79d08db5bd09a25%7Cb71ff3f628164ca8a9b938f820f91ad1%7C0%7C0%7C638204723732367131%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C3000%7C%7C%7C&amp;amp;sdata=9DgboiHTFPrNYVhdKhyfdwVyNYwUvZbP%2FroLdWIIfxw%3D&amp;amp;reserved=0&quot;&gt;Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;For CA applicants, please also refer to our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://nam12.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.precisionmedicinegrp.com%2Fca-applicants-privacy-notice%2F&amp;amp;data=05%7C01%7Czeta.larcon%40precisionmedicinegrp.com%7Cb58fe8b0c3ea4dd2e79d08db5bd09a25%7Cb71ff3f628164ca8a9b938f820f91ad1%7C0%7C0%7C638204723732367131%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C3000%7C%7C%7C&amp;amp;sdata=tfAqqMZsG%2B11IchL45HFFVbfECCkYqQpNr0PQxrMFJU%3D&amp;amp;reserved=0&quot;&gt;CA Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
